00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.469
BETH: While not all children with
autism have speech and language

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:08.600
delays, autism frequently causes
social communication challenges and

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.799
therefore delays in social development.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:17.059
Children with autism may have a harder
time using or understanding non-verbal

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.289
communication such as pointing and
smiling and conversation tends to

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:24.859
come across with little animation
or inflection in their speech.

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:28.680
JOE: Individuals with High
functioning Autism can use language

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.410
to communicate with other people.

00:00:30.889 --> 00:00:34.470
But their core communication problems,
often make it impossible for them

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.750
to learn language in the normal
way, which relies heavily on social

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.019
context, and non-verbal communications.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:44.960
They may be more motivated by
their own interests rather than

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.370
by social responses and may rarely
or never imitate others' actions.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.949
BETH: Some individuals with autism use
language intellectually and are highly

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:58.390
literal in how they use and understand
it, in contrast to the figurative

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.600
way most other people use language.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:06.000
They find it difficult to understand
and rarely use sarcasm and irony and

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.330
other forms of communication where one
thing is said while another is meant.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.824
JOE: Because of their difficulty
understanding body language and

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:18.329
nonverbal communication they often
cannot pick up on hints and clues that

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:22.679
people drop to indicate interest or
disinterest in what is being discussed

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.160
or an activity that is happening.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.569
BETH: People with the most severe cases of
autism spectrum disorder typically require

00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:32.090
very substantial support from others.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.390
They may be completely isolated.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.720
They may not use language at all,
or they may even be very limited

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.480
in their ability to communicate.

